ncyclopedia/odisha">Orissa</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1773</span><span class="rf-text">The Regulating Act 1773 made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warren-hastings">Warren Hastings</a> Governor-General of Fort William and placed the Company under parliamentary oversight</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1793</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-cornwallis-1st-marquess-cornwallis">Lord Cornwallis</a> promulgated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/permanent-settlement">Permanent Settlement</a> of land revenue in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1818</span><span class="rf-text">The Anglo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> wars ended, leaving no native power that threatened the Company</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1833</span><span class="rf-text">The Saint Helena Act ended the Company's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> monopoly and made it an agent for the administration of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-india">British India</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1849–1856</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> was annexed after the Anglo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> Wars, followed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berar">Berar</a> in 1854 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/awadh">Oudh</a> in 1856</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1857–1858</span><span class="rf-text">The Indian rebellion of 1857 was followed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/government-of-india-act-1858">Government of India Act 1858</a>, which ended Company rule</span></li></ol>
